@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- AIA An Phuc Tron Doi Uu Viet: product rules and terms, version V082021.
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../source/raw/aia-an-phuc.txt, the `pdftotext -layout` rendering of
-- TC-APTDUV-Quy-tac-dieu-khoan-mau.pdf (sha256 of the PDF c73c035e...f8b844), retrieved
-- 2026-10-06 from aia.com.vn. This module quotes no clause: each clause is quoted, as
-- generated `src:N` lines, beside the rule that encodes it, and the comments here give its line
-- numbers. Vietnamese words in comments are copied from the source and checked by tools/vnsrc.py.
--
-- Money is Vietnamese dong (VND), a bare NUMBER. A rate is a NUMBER (5% is 0.05).
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the
-- fact, or the certificate, the Company's records or a medical record shows it. Whether the
-- fact makes a benefit payable is a rule, and belongs in the chapter module that says so.

§ `Nouns for the An Phuc Tron Doi Uu Viet rules and terms`

§§ `The parties`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 233, 236-237, 240-241, 244, 250)
-- The four defined parties (1.1 to 1.4), and the claimant of Chapter 7, as actors for the
-- regulative rules (the Company's duty to settle a claim, the policyholder's free-look right).
DECLARE `A party` IS ONE OF
    `the Company`
    `the policyholder`
    `the insured`
    `a beneficiary`
    `the claimant`

-- The acts those rules speak of.
DECLARE `An act under the contract` IS ONE OF
    `refuse to continue the insurance`
    `refund the premiums paid, without interest, less medical examination costs`
    `settle the claim`
    `settle the claim with interest on the amount paid late`

§§ `The policyholder`

-- 1.2: an individual aged 18 or more with full civil act capacity, or an organisation, who
-- declares and signs the application and pays the premium. `date of birth` is NOTHING for an
-- organisation. Whether the person has full civil act capacity is a matter of record.
DECLARE `A policyholder` HAS
    `an organisation`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of birth`                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `full civil act capacity`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared and signed the application` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The insured and the policyholder's insurable interest`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 240-242)
DECLARE `An insured person` HAS
    `date of birth`                                       IS A DATE
    `living in Vietnam when the application was submitted` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 2.2: the persons in whom the policyholder has an insurable interest, one constructor per
-- bullet, in the source's order. The grandparent condition of the fourth bullet is part of
-- its constructor. The last bullet sends the reader to the Law on Insurance Business, which
-- this encoding does not encode.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 579, 585-586, 592, 598, 602-603, 605-607)
DECLARE `A relationship of the insured to the policyholder` IS ONE OF
    `the policyholder themself`
    `a natural parent, lawful spouse, or natural or lawfully adopted child`
    `a natural sibling`
    `a natural grandchild, the policyholder being a grandparent`
    `a person in a relationship of nurture or support`
    `a lawful guardian`
    `another person`

-- The application, as submitted (Article 2, 1.6, Article 5).
-- `date the first basic premium was paid in full` is NOTHING until it is paid.
DECLARE `An application` HAS
    `the policyholder`                                IS A `A policyholder`
    `the insured`                                     IS AN `An insured person`
    `relationship of the insured to the policyholder` IS A `A relationship of the insured to the policyholder`
    `date the application was completed`              IS A DATE
    `date the first basic premium was paid in full`   IS A MAYBE DATE
    `accepted by the Company`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed in person by the insured`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by a parent or guardian of the insured, on the application or another consent` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The contract, as the certificate and the Company's records show it`

-- `effective date`: 1.6, shown on the certificate.
-- `date the Company accepted the insurance`: the acceptance date that 1.30 and 6.3 count from;
--   it is not the effective date, which 1.6 fixes earlier, at completion and first payment.
-- `date of the last reinstatement`: Article 24 makes a reinstatement effective on the date the
--   Company approves it; 1.30, 6.3 and 8.1 count from the most recent one. NOTHING if none.
-- `date of the last increase of the current sum insured`: 6.3. NOTHING if none.
-- `annualised basic premium of the first contract year`: 1.16 caps accumulation premiums at
--   five times the first contract year's basic premium on the annual mode (src:359, 365).
--   The document gives no modal factors, so the annual-mode figure is read from the certificate.
-- `accepted on standard terms at issue or at the last reinstatement`: 11.1, third bullet.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 267-268, 270-271)
DECLARE `The contract` HAS
    `effective date`                                              IS A DATE
    `date the Company accepted the insurance`                     IS A DATE
    `date of the last reinstatement`                              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date of the last increase of the current sum insured`        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `insured's date of birth`                                     IS A DATE
    `premium mode`                                                IS A `A premium mode`
    `annualised basic premium of the first contract year`         IS A NUMBER
    `accepted on standard terms at issue or at the last reinstatement` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 14.2: the four modes in which the basic premium may be paid.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1455)
DECLARE `A premium mode` IS ONE OF
    annual
    `semi-annual`
    quarterly
    monthly

-- 7.2.1: the two death and disability benefits the policyholder chooses between, shown on
-- the certificate; Article 12 lets the choice be switched once.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 894, 907)
DECLARE `A benefit option` IS ONE OF
    `the basic benefit`
    `the enhanced benefit`

-- The contract as it stands at one moment (a claim, a request, a monthiversary).
-- `cancer benefit already paid`: the 7.5 amount paid earlier under this contract, 0 if none.
-- `outstanding debts`: 1.28, premiums and charges due and unpaid and any other amount owed.
DECLARE `The state of the contract` HAS
    `in force`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `benefit option`               IS A `A benefit option`
    `current sum insured`          IS A NUMBER
    `basic account value`          IS A NUMBER
    `accumulation account value`   IS A NUMBER
    `outstanding debts`            IS A NUMBER
    `cancer benefit already paid`  IS A NUMBER

§§ `The insured events`

-- The facts 8.1 turns on, shared by a death and a disability.
-- `date the cause first existed`: the date the cause that led to the death or disability
--   first existed (a diagnosis, an injury, an accident). 8.1, third bullet, compares it with
--   the effective date and the date of the last reinstatement.
-- `an act of insurance fraud`: 1.33 defines fraud by reference to the Criminal Code; whether
--   an act was one is a finding of the authorities, recorded as an input.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1137, 1139-1141, 1145-1146)
DECLARE `The cause of a death or disability` HAS
    `an act of insurance fraud`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `suicide or attempted suicide` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date the cause first existed` IS A DATE
    `war`                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- 1.31: an Accident. The three qualities the definition requires are recorded as found.
-- `excluded circumstances`: every circumstance listed in 8.2 of which the death was a direct
-- or indirect consequence; EMPTY if none.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 539-544)
DECLARE `An accident` HAS
    `date of the accident`                                        IS A DATE
    `by the impact of a sudden, external force or object`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `unintended and against the will of the insured`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the direct and sole cause, unrelated to any other cause`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded circumstances`                                      IS A LIST OF `A circumstance listed in 8.2`

-- 8.2, one constructor per circumstance, in the source's order. The dangerous recreational
-- activities are listed after "như:" (such as), so the list is open; an activity that is not
-- named is `another recreational activity said to be dangerous`.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1185, 1189, 1191, 1197, 1207, 1214-1217, 1219-1220)
DECLARE `A circumstance listed in 8.2` IS ONE OF
    `an intentional act of the policyholder`
    `an intentional act of the insured`
    `an intentional act of a beneficiary`
    `war, armed conflict, riot, disturbance, strike or terrorism`
    `fighting or brawling, or resisting arrest by the competent authority`
    `use of stimulants or drugs, suicide, or deliberate self-injury`
    `alcohol above the legal limit, or the effect of medication not prescribed`
    `an accident in an aircraft, other than as a passenger on a scheduled commercial flight`
    `scuba diving`
    `bungee jumping`
    `parachuting`
    `mountain climbing`
    `horse racing or vehicle racing`
    `an unnecessary dangerous act, other than to save a life`
    `another recreational activity said to be dangerous`
    `radioactive material`

-- 1.4 and 26.2: a beneficiary named by the policyholder.
-- `designated share`: the beneficiary's share of the death benefit, as a fraction.
-- `took part in the intentional act`: 8.2, first bullet, second sentence.
DECLARE `A beneficiary` HAS
    `name`                             IS A STRING
    `designated share`                 IS A NUMBER
    `died before the insured`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `took part in the intentional act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A death. `the accident` is NOTHING where the death was not caused by an accident.
-- `determined to be a non-smoker`: 7.3 does not say who determines it or when; the
--   determination is recorded as an input (NOTES.md, fork F23).
-- `premiums received after the death`: 7.2.2 refunds them.
DECLARE `A death` HAS
    `date of death`                   IS A DATE
    `the cause`                       IS A `The cause of a death or disability`
    `the accident`                    IS A MAYBE `An accident`
    `determined to be a non-smoker`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `premiums received after the death` IS A NUMBER
    `the beneficiaries`               IS A LIST OF `A beneficiary`
    `the policyholder has died`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- 1.29(b): who certified the disability rate. The first two are the bodies 1.29(b) names;
-- the third is the one 27.1 names in the list of claim documents.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 460-462, 2215, 2221-2222)
DECLARE `A certifying body` IS ONE OF
    `a provincial or centrally-run city medical assessment council`
    `an independent medical organisation approved by the Company`
    `a lawful foreign medical organisation approved by the Company`
    `another body`

-- 1.29: a disability.
-- (a) the counts of hands lost at or above the wrist, legs lost at or above the ankle (or
--     wholly and irrecoverably paralysed), and eyes lost or wholly and irrecoverably blind.
-- (b) the rate certified, by whom, and when. NOTHING where there is no certification.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 443-447, 453-458)
DECLARE `A disability` HAS
    `date of the disability`                         IS A DATE
    `hands lost or irrecoverably paralysed`          IS A NUMBER
    `legs lost or irrecoverably paralysed`           IS A NUMBER
    `eyes totally and permanently blind`             IS A NUMBER
    `certified rate of disability or of permanent loss of working capacity` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `certified by`                                   IS A `A certifying body`
    `date of the certification`                      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the cause`                                      IS A `The cause of a death or disability`

-- 1.30: a cancer, as the medical record describes it.
-- `date the cancer arose`: 1.30 says a cancer arises when it is examined, diagnosed or treated,
--   or when signs or symptoms appear that would lead an ordinary person to seek medical care;
--   the earliest of those, as the record shows it.
-- The five exclusions (a) to (e), each as the histology or staging records it.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 465-466, 472-474, 480-481, 487, 490-491, 493-494, 497-498, 503-504, 510)
DECLARE `A cancer` HAS
    `a malignant tumour confirmed by histology, growing uncontrollably and invading tissue` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date the cancer arose`                                        IS A DATE
    `pre-malignant, non-invasive or in situ, or of borderline or low malignancy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a tumour of the prostate, thyroid or bladder classified T1N0M0` IS A BOOLEAN
    `chronic lymphocytic leukaemia`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `RAI stage`                                                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `in the presence of HIV infection`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a skin cancer`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `malignant melanoma`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `Breslow depth in millimetres`                                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `Clark level`                                                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- 7.4 and 7.5 cap the benefits across all the insured's contracts with the Company, at a
-- limit that "có thể được điều chỉnh tăng" and is published on the Company's website.
-- `limit published at the time of payment`: NOTHING where no increase has been published,
-- and the printed 10 billion dong applies.
-- `the same kind of benefit already received under all contracts with the Company`: for 7.4,
-- accidental-death benefits under the other contracts; for 7.5, critical-illness and cancer
-- benefits already received.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 977, 984-987)
DECLARE `The aggregate limit at the time of payment` HAS
    `limit published at the time of payment`                              IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the same kind of benefit already received under all contracts with the Company` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Temporary insurance (Article 5)`

-- `date the temporary cover ended`: 5.2, the earliest of the certificate's issue, the
--   refusal, and the policyholder's cancellation of the application; NOTHING if none yet.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 655-658, 665-667)
DECLARE `A death during temporary insurance` HAS
    `date the application was completed and the first premium paid in full` IS A DATE
    `date the temporary cover ended`                                       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date of death`                                                        IS A DATE
    `the accident`                                                         IS A MAYBE `An accident`
    `suicide`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `total sum insured of all applications for the same insured`           IS A NUMBER
    `total first premiums paid on all applications for the same insured`   IS A NUMBER
    `medical examination costs`                                            IS A NUMBER

§§ `Disclosure (6.2, 6.3, 6.5)`

-- 6.2: what the Company would have done with correct information.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 709-710, 715, 723-724)
DECLARE `What the Company would have done with correct information` IS ONE OF
    `declined to insure the insured`
    `insured with limited benefits or an extra premium`
    `insured on the same terms`

-- 6.2: what the Company may do, one constructor per remedy, in the source's order.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 715-716, 722, 730, 736-737, 743, 749)
DECLARE `A remedy under 6.2` IS ONE OF
    `refuse the benefit, end the contract and keep the premiums up to the end`
    `pay the benefit in full after collecting or deducting the premium increase`
    `pay a sum insured reduced in proportion to the premium paid`
    `refuse the part of the benefit beyond the insurable limit`

DECLARE `A misstatement` HAS
    `intentional`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `with correct information the Company would have` IS A `What the Company would have done with correct information`

-- 6.5(a): the purposes for which the Company may collect, use and transfer the information
-- without consent; one constructor per purpose, in the source's order.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 808-812, 818)
DECLARE `A purpose of a transfer of information` IS ONE OF
    `a request of a competent state authority`
    `underwriting, premium calculation, issue of the contract or premium collection`
    `reinsurance or technical reserves`
    `settling claims`
    `product research and design, or preventing insurance fraud`
    `research and assessment of financial position, solvency, capital adequacy or capital requirements`
    `storing, processing and administering the database`
    `another purpose`

DECLARE `A transfer of information to a third party` HAS
    `purpose`                                         IS A `A purpose of a transfer of information`
    `written consent of the policyholder or the insured` IS A BOOLEAN
    `told the purpose and given the choice to consent or not` IS A BOOLEAN
    `refusal of consent used to refuse to conclude the contract` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Premiums and the account value (Chapter 4)`

-- One payment, applied under 14.5.1 (contract years 1 to 4) or 14.5.2 (from year 5).
-- `basic premium due` and `rider premiums due`: the periodic amounts due at this due date.
-- `basic and rider premiums of the contract year still to fall due after this one`: what
--   remains of the year's premiums once this instalment is paid; 0 for an annual payer, or
--   for the year's last instalment. 14.5.1(iv) and 14.5.2(iii) turn on it.
-- `accumulation premiums already received in the contract year`: for the 1.16 cap.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1482, 1484-1485, 1488-1490, 1495-1496)
DECLARE `A premium payment` HAS
    `contract year`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `amount paid`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `basic premium due`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `rider premiums due`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `basic and rider premiums of the contract year still to fall due after this one` IS A NUMBER
    `accumulation premiums already received in the contract year`    IS A NUMBER

-- What 14.5 makes of a payment.
DECLARE `A grace period that 14.5 opens` IS ONE OF
    `no grace period`
    `the 60-day grace period for the supplementary products`
    `the grace period for the contract under 15.1`

DECLARE `The application of a payment` HAS
    `applied to the basic premium`      IS A NUMBER
    `applied or held for the rider premiums` IS A NUMBER
    `counted as accumulation premium`   IS A NUMBER
    `grace period opened`               IS A `A grace period that 14.5 opens`

-- One month on the two accounts, from the previous monthiversary to this one (16.1(b),
-- 16.2(b)). Every figure is the month's, as the Company's records show it.
-- `premium year of the basic premiums paid`: the premium year (1.12) to which they belong,
--   which selects the allocation rate of 14.5.3.
-- Interest is an input: 16.1(b)(iii) and 16.2(b)(iii) credit "Tiền lãi tính theo Lãi suất
--   tích lũy của tháng trước" but do not say on what balance or how a yearly rate becomes a
--   monthly one (NOTES.md, fork F18).
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1717, 1723, 1729-1735)
DECLARE `A month on the account` HAS
    `basic account value at the previous monthiversary`                 IS A NUMBER
    `accumulation account value at the previous monthiversary`          IS A NUMBER
    `basic premiums paid since the previous monthiversary`              IS A NUMBER
    `premium year of the basic premiums paid`                           IS A NUMBER
    `accumulation premiums paid since the previous monthiversary`       IS A NUMBER
    `interest on the basic account value at the previous month's rate`  IS A NUMBER
    `interest on the accumulation account value at the previous month's rate` IS A NUMBER
    `cost of insurance for the month`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `contract administration charge for the month`                      IS A NUMBER
    `withdrawals from the basic account value since the previous monthiversary` IS A NUMBER
    `withdrawals from the accumulation account value since the previous monthiversary` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `The account at a monthiversary` HAS
    `basic account value`             IS A NUMBER
    `accumulation account value`      IS A NUMBER
    `monthly deduction left unpaid`   IS A NUMBER

-- 15.1: the two events that open the contract's grace period. NOTHING where the event has
-- not happened.
-- `basic premiums of the first four contract years all paid in full` and
-- `a withdrawal from the basic account value ever made`: the two conditions of 15.4.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1661-1666)
DECLARE `The premium history` HAS
    `due date of a basic premium not paid in full, in the first four contract years` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the account value fell short of the monthly deduction, from the fifth contract year` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `basic premiums of the first four contract years all paid in full`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a withdrawal from the basic account value ever made`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `date the required premium was paid`                                  IS A MAYBE DATE

-- 7.7: the loyalty bonus. `interest credited to the basic account value, by contract year`
-- lists the interest credited in contract years 1, 2, 3, ... in that order.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1041-1043, 1049, 1055-1056, 1062)
DECLARE `The record for the loyalty bonus` HAS
    `interest credited to the basic account value, by contract year`  IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `basic premiums of earlier contract years paid in full at each due date, grace period included` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the two most recent monthly basic premiums paid in full before the bonus date` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The policyholder's requests (Chapter 3)`

-- 9.1: a request to withdraw from the account value.
-- `minimum set by the Company at the time`: "hạn mức tối thiểu do Công ty quy định tại từng
-- thời điểm", not in the document.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1251-1255)
DECLARE `A withdrawal request` HAS
    `date of the request`                     IS A DATE
    `amount requested`                        IS A NUMBER
    `minimum set by the Company at the time`  IS A NUMBER

-- Article 10: a request to increase or decrease the sum insured. The maximum and the minimum
-- are set by the Company from time to time and are not in the document.
DECLARE `A request to change the sum insured` HAS
    `date of the request`                        IS A DATE
    `new sum insured`                            IS A NUMBER
    `maximum set by the Company at the time`     IS A NUMBER
    `minimum set by the Company at the time`     IS A NUMBER
    `date of the Company's written approval`     IS A MAYBE DATE

-- Article 11: a request to increase the current sum insured without evidence of health or
-- finances, on the insured's marriage or the birth of the insured's child.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1318-1326, 1334)
DECLARE `A request to increase the sum insured on marriage or a birth` HAS
    `date of the request`                                      IS A DATE
    `date of the marriage or the birth`                        IS A DATE
    `increase requested`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `proof of the marriage or the birth submitted`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `increases already made under Article 11`                     IS A NUMBER
    `total sum insured under all contracts with the Company after the increase` IS A NUMBER
    `maximum set by the Company at the time`                   IS A NUMBER
    `date of the Company's approval`                           IS A MAYBE DATE

-- Article 12: a request to switch between the two benefit options.
DECLARE `A request to switch the benefit option` HAS
    `date of the request`             IS A DATE
    `switches already made`           IS A NUMBER
    `date of the Company's approval`  IS A MAYBE DATE

-- 13.1: a request to add a supplementary product.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1423-1426)
DECLARE `A request to add a supplementary product` HAS
    `the Company offers the product at the time`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the policyholder and the insured are eligible for it`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the policyholder agrees to pay its additional premium`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of the Company's written approval`                         IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `Change, reinstatement and termination (Chapter 6)`

-- Article 21: the free-look refusal.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1888-1891)
DECLARE `A free-look refusal` HAS
    `date the contract was issued`                IS A DATE
    `date the policyholder received the contract` IS A DATE
    `date of the refusal`                         IS A DATE
    `premiums paid`                               IS A NUMBER
    `medical examination costs`                   IS A NUMBER

-- 22.3: what the Company may do when the insured no longer resides in Vietnam, one
-- constructor per option, in the source's order.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 1944-1945, 1951, 1957-1959)
DECLARE `A step open to the Company under 22.3` IS ONE OF
    `raise the cost of insurance or the basic premium`
    `reduce the sum insured`
    `cancel the supplementary products`
    `end the contract, paying the account value less the debts`

-- Article 23: a misstatement of the insured's age or sex.
-- `cost of insurance due on the true age and sex` and `cost of insurance deducted`: the
-- totals to date, from the Company's records and its rate table (Article 18).
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 2005-2007)
DECLARE `A misstatement of age or sex` HAS
    `true date of birth`                              IS A DATE
    `cost of insurance due on the true age and sex`  IS A NUMBER
    `cost of insurance deducted`                     IS A NUMBER
    `premiums paid`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `medical examination costs`                      IS A NUMBER
    `withdrawals from the account value`             IS A NUMBER
    `benefits already paid`                          IS A NUMBER

-- Article 24: a request to reinstate a lapsed contract.
-- `contract year in which it lapsed`: 24(i) and (ii) turn on it.
-- `all overdue basic premiums of the compulsory payment period paid`: 24(i); the document
--   does not define "thời gian đóng phí bắt buộc" (NOTES.md, finding).
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 2074, 2080-2090)
DECLARE `A reinstatement request` HAS
    `date the contract lapsed`                              IS A DATE
    `contract year in which it lapsed`                      IS A NUMBER
    `date of the written request`                           IS A DATE
    `all overdue basic premiums of the compulsory payment period paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `basic premium instalments due at reinstatement paid`   IS A NUMBER
    `evidence of health given and every insurability condition met` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of the Company's approval`                        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the policyholder and the insured alive at the approval` IS A BOOLEAN

-- 25.2: the events on which the contract ends automatically, one constructor per limb.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 2111-2113, 2119-2120, 2126)
DECLARE `An event that ends the contract` IS ONE OF
    `the insured dies`
    `the Company approves payment of the disability benefit`
    `the maturity date arrives`
    `the contract has been lapsed for more than 24 months in a row`
    `another case provided by law`

§§ `Claims (Chapter 7)`

-- Article 26: who is paid.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 2172-2174, 2176-2178)
DECLARE `A payee` IS ONE OF
    `the beneficiary named` HAS `name` IS A STRING
    `the policyholder`
    `the policyholder's lawful heirs`

-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 2201, 2253)
DECLARE `A kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `a death claim`
    `a disability claim`
    `a cancer claim`
    `a maturity claim`

-- 27.1 and 27.2: the documents submitted, one field per document the clauses list.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 2208-2209, 2214-2215, 2221-2222, 2228-2229, 2235-2236, 2242, 2248-2251, 2257-2259)
DECLARE `The documents submitted` HAS
    `claim form completed fully and accurately`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `extract of the death record`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `certificate of the injury rate from the medical assessment council or an approved foreign medical organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `medical evidence from the examining, diagnosing or treating doctor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accident record, scene examination record, forensic and investigation conclusions certified by the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proof of the right to the benefit, such as a will, and identity papers of the person entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proof of the right to receive the benefit, such as an authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A claim, with the dates Chapter 7 counts from.
-- `days spent supplying documents under 27.3 and 27.4`: Article 28 does not count that time.
-- `date the complete and valid file was received`: Article 29's 30 days run from it.
DECLARE `A claim` HAS
    `kind`                                                 IS A `A kind of claim`
    `caused by an accident`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of the insured event`                            IS A DATE
    `date the claim was made`                              IS A DATE
    `days spent supplying documents under 27.3 and 27.4`   IS A NUMBER
    `the documents`                                        IS A `The documents submitted`
    `date the complete and valid file was received`        IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `The universal-life fund and disputes (Chapters 8 and 9)`

-- Article 31: the assets the Company says it will choose.
-- (the clause is quoted where its rule is; source lines 2350-2352)
DECLARE `An investment asset` IS ONE OF
    `government bonds`
    `municipal bonds`
    `corporate bonds`
    `bank deposits`
    `another asset`
